*Example 2 — <<<source:>>> (custom AbstractManagedObjectSource)

  When a managed object needs to declare flows or perform asynchronous setup, implement
  {{{/apidocs/net/officefloor/frame/api/managedobject/source/impl/AbstractManagedObjectSource.html}AbstractManagedObjectSource}}
  directly and reference the class via <<<source:>>> in the YAML.
  {{{/apidocs/net/officefloor/frame/api/build/None.html}None}} is used as the type
  parameter for the dependency keys when the source has no dependencies.


**The managed object value class

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/java/net/officefloor/tutorial/springrestmanagedobject/SessionId.java|ignoreDownloadError=false}


**The ManagedObjectSource

  <<<SessionIdSource>>> extends
  {{{/apidocs/net/officefloor/frame/api/managedobject/source/impl/AbstractManagedObjectSource.html}AbstractManagedObjectSource}}
  with {{{/apidocs/net/officefloor/frame/api/build/None.html}None}} for dependencies (no
  other objects required) and <<<Flows>>> for the one declared output:

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/java/net/officefloor/tutorial/springrestmanagedobject/SessionIdSource.java|ignoreDownloadError=false}

  OfficeFloor requires every flow declared via <<<context.addFlow()>>> to be wired to a
  handler in the YAML.  A source triggers the flow at runtime via
  {{{/apidocs/net/officefloor/frame/api/managedobject/source/ManagedObjectExecuteContext.html}ManagedObjectExecuteContext.invokeStartupProcess()}}
  (on application start) or via
  {{{/apidocs/net/officefloor/frame/api/managedobject/source/ManagedObjectUser.html}ManagedObjectUser.setManagedObject()}}
  for per-request asynchronous completion.


**The flow handler

  <<<SessionLogService>>> is wired to the <<<LOG>>> flow.  The
  {{{/apidocs/net/officefloor/plugin/section/clazz/Parameter.html}@Parameter}} annotation
  receives the typed argument the source passes when it triggers the flow:

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/java/net/officefloor/tutorial/springrestmanagedobject/SessionLogService.java|ignoreDownloadError=false}


